WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:02.550
Is everyone here?

00:03.200 --> 00:05.210
It's been a while since all 
our top officers were here,

00:05.210 --> 00:08.780
so before the festival, I think we should 
have a debriefing on what's been going on.

00:08.780 --> 00:10.930
I have some introductions to make, too.

00:10.930 --> 00:11.650
Right.

00:12.290 --> 00:13.990
Hey, where's Milim?

00:13.990 --> 00:15.860
Oh, she went home.

00:16.280 --> 00:16.910
Bye!

00:16.910 --> 00:21.240
If she stayed in Tempest any longer, 
she'd get in trouble with Frey.

00:21.240 --> 00:22.490
Ah, right.

00:23.810 --> 00:25.800
Okay, first, let me introduce this guy.

00:26.180 --> 00:27.560
This is Mjöllmile-kun.

00:29.820 --> 00:31.730
I know some of you are 
seeing him for the first time,

00:31.730 --> 00:33.510
but he's a capable man.

00:33.680 --> 00:35.310
If the festival's a success,

00:35.310 --> 00:38.660
I'm thinking of putting him in 
charge of our country's finances.

00:40.220 --> 00:42.540
My name is Gard Mjöllmile.

00:42.540 --> 00:45.090
Now that Great Rimuru 
has given me this grand task,

00:45.090 --> 00:47.190
I intend to tackle it with due seriousness.

00:47.190 --> 00:49.010
I hope you'll all be good to me.

00:49.760 --> 00:51.650
Well, now that they know who you are...

00:51.650 --> 00:53.860
I'll leave the rest to you, Mjöllmile-kun.

00:54.380 --> 00:56.700
Right. Well, then, if I may...

00:57.110 --> 01:01.960
I, the humble Mjöllmile, 
will now give a full run-down

01:01.200 --> 01:04.960
<b>Nation's Opening Festival Schedule</b>

01:01.960 --> 01:04.440
on the festival to celebrate 
this nation's opening.

02:08.600 --> 02:13.150
<b>That Time I Got Reincarnated as a Slime</b>

02:35.410 --> 02:38.620
In two days, the night 
before the opening ceremony,

02:35.800 --> 02:40.180
<b>Episode 65: The Lightspeed Hero</b>

02:38.620 --> 02:41.340
we will hold a national 
Festival Eve celebration.

02:42.410 --> 02:45.250
Throughout the festival, 
we will host not only invited guests,

02:45.250 --> 02:50.460
but merchants passing through Tempest 
and the adventurers escorting them,

02:50.460 --> 02:53.730
as well as provide them with food 
and drink, all free of charge.

02:53.930 --> 02:56.480
Wow, that'll be one lavish feast.

02:57.310 --> 02:58.240
And...

02:58.450 --> 03:03.380
We will hold a palace banquet in the 
reception hall for royalty and nobility.

03:03.750 --> 03:09.120
Princess Shuna and Mr. Yoshida will 
work together to prepare the feast.

03:09.120 --> 03:10.880
I hear there'll be new dishes on the menu?

03:11.090 --> 03:13.620
Yes. Do look forward to it.

03:13.620 --> 03:14.210
So excited!

03:14.210 --> 03:16.930
And day one of the main event, 
the Opening Festival,

03:16.930 --> 03:20.000
will be kicked off with a speech 
from Great Rimuru himself!

03:20.000 --> 03:21.320
Again?

03:21.600 --> 03:23.790
Everyone already knows I'm a Demon Lord now.

03:23.790 --> 03:25.260
Do I really have to?

03:25.470 --> 03:26.760
You do!

03:27.910 --> 03:30.510
Okay, fine.

03:30.960 --> 03:31.770
And then?

03:32.220 --> 03:34.360
After the speech, Great Rimuru will enjoy

03:34.360 --> 03:39.860
the inaugural performance at 
the newly opened Tempest Opera.

03:40.140 --> 03:41.810
Oh? Opera?

03:41.810 --> 03:42.830
I see.

03:43.610 --> 03:46.370
The goal is to show all nations and lands

03:46.370 --> 03:48.360
that Great Rimuru is a marvelous Demon Lord

03:48.360 --> 03:51.960
who is well-versed in culture 
and the arts, yes?

03:52.190 --> 03:53.690
Right on the money.

03:53.690 --> 03:55.690
What kind of performance will it be?

03:55.690 --> 03:58.150
You'll find out when the day comes.

04:00.460 --> 04:01.630
<i>They wouldn't...</i>

04:02.250 --> 04:05.510
Then, after lunch will be a 
presentation of the nation's technology.

04:05.510 --> 04:09.710
Gabiru and Vesta will explain 
the history of their healing potions,

04:09.710 --> 04:14.770
and Kurobe and Garm will display some 
of the equipment they've made.

04:15.040 --> 04:16.330
And on day two,

04:16.330 --> 04:19.770
the martial arts tournament 
will begin at the colosseum.

04:19.960 --> 04:25.180
After midday, our guests will 
be free to roam about as they please.

04:25.530 --> 04:29.080
They can enjoy the hot springs 
that our nation is so proud of,

04:29.080 --> 04:32.040
or stay and watch the 
martial arts tournament,

04:32.040 --> 04:34.920
or enjoy the various stalls 
set up throughout the festival.

04:37.080 --> 04:40.920
Look forward to the best-tasting 
grilled dishes you've ever seen!

04:41.310 --> 04:42.900
And, um, what about me?

04:42.900 --> 04:45.920
You will be in the VIP seating at the arena.

04:45.920 --> 04:49.910
I was thinking we would allow people 
who wanted an audience with you

04:49.910 --> 04:52.180
to come in and meet you there.

04:53.280 --> 04:56.700
Okay, so I can just enjoy 
the martial arts tournament.

04:56.930 --> 04:58.480
Sounds like we're all ready.

04:58.480 --> 05:00.320
Yes! And on day two,

05:00.560 --> 05:04.120
we will, at long last, 
reveal our new dungeon!

05:04.790 --> 05:05.990
Even without me here,

05:06.360 --> 05:09.370
it seems you've built a fine colosseum.

05:09.550 --> 05:13.270
Yeah, all thanks to the hard 
work you and Gobkyu put in.

05:13.760 --> 05:16.080
Everything's going as planned so far.

05:17.460 --> 05:19.910
Do any of you have any problems to bring up?

05:20.330 --> 05:21.590
Yes! I do!

05:21.940 --> 05:23.090
Ramiris?

05:23.090 --> 05:24.160
Yeah, so...

05:24.670 --> 05:26.320
I have a problem!

05:29.560 --> 05:30.720
Well, you know...

05:30.720 --> 05:34.390
There's a forest on floor 95 
of the dungeon, right?

05:34.390 --> 05:37.930
For some reason, it's begun 
to encroach upon the floors above it.

05:37.930 --> 05:41.370
It's already overtaken all 
the floors up to 71.

05:41.370 --> 05:42.730
It overtook them?!

05:43.280 --> 05:45.460
There are no monsters 
suitable to serve as bosses.

05:45.460 --> 05:46.070
Huh?

05:46.840 --> 05:50.950
The encroaching trees have consumed 
more magicules than expected,

05:50.950 --> 05:54.200
and no monsters fit to be 
bosses have been generated.

05:54.320 --> 05:59.210
Yeah, so I want to make 
another Elemental Colossus.

05:59.210 --> 06:02.230
So I want you to get me 
the materials I need!

06:02.230 --> 06:04.660
And I desire someone worthy of being a boss!

06:04.660 --> 06:07.170
And for someone to clean my virgin forest!

06:07.820 --> 06:11.110
Uh, can't you guys do something 
about that yourselves?

06:11.110 --> 06:12.200
Master!

06:12.830 --> 06:14.560
I know someone worthy.

06:14.560 --> 06:16.080
You do?

06:16.080 --> 06:18.820
The mystic fox I've been caring 
for has awakened.

06:20.330 --> 06:22.060
I-It's so cute!

06:22.480 --> 06:26.080
Developing forests is what I do best!

06:26.080 --> 06:28.080
I thought it might be 
amusing to let her do it.

06:29.380 --> 06:32.290
Right. You want to give it a try?

06:33.570 --> 06:35.530
I very much do!

06:35.530 --> 06:37.070
Okay, then...

06:37.070 --> 06:40.060
Oh! I should give you a name.

06:41.200 --> 06:43.220
"Yoko" just means "mystic fox," 
so that's boring...

06:43.220 --> 06:48.120
and the name "Nine Head" that Clayman 
used would be wasted on your cute looks.

06:50.240 --> 06:51.340
I got it!

06:51.810 --> 06:53.690
From now on, your name is Kumara!

06:54.130 --> 06:55.380
Oh, wait...

06:55.380 --> 06:56.230
<i>Notice.</i>

06:56.230 --> 06:57.850
<i>This is an effect of naming.</i>

06:58.350 --> 07:02.160
<i>Because the individual called Kumara 
already possessed tremendous energy,</i>

07:00.350 --> 07:02.230
Expected Amount

07:02.160 --> 07:04.680
<i>you lost a great deal more than expected.</i>

07:02.230 --> 07:05.110
Actual Amount

07:05.400 --> 07:08.440
<i>Really? Her looks sure fooled me...</i>

07:13.940 --> 07:15.710
Thank you kindly!

07:15.710 --> 07:17.660
I'll be counting on you, Kumara.

07:17.660 --> 07:19.180
I will do my very best!

07:19.180 --> 07:19.660
Good.

07:19.830 --> 07:20.920
Great Rimuru.

07:21.660 --> 07:24.170
We have a recommendation, as well.

07:24.470 --> 07:27.440
We know someone who would 
make the perfect boss.

07:29.520 --> 07:30.640
I see.

07:30.950 --> 07:34.940
Okay, we'll go with Shuna and 
Treyni-san's idea for the new dungeon boss.

07:35.440 --> 07:39.680
And that concludes my explanation 
of the Opening Festival.

07:39.960 --> 07:41.790
Yeah, good work.

07:41.790 --> 07:42.360
Thank you.

07:42.810 --> 07:47.240
Next, let's hear the 
report I asked Soei for.

07:47.240 --> 07:47.810
Right.

07:48.240 --> 07:52.200
First of all, Viscount Kazak of the 
Kingdom of Blumund has been arrested.

07:52.870 --> 07:55.950
It seems the viscount was 
a leading officer in Orthrus.

07:56.110 --> 07:57.840
Wh-What?!

07:57.840 --> 07:59.080
Orthrus?

07:59.340 --> 08:01.240
A bunch of savage,

08:01.240 --> 08:04.450
heinous slave traders who disgrace 
the name of merchants everywhere.

08:04.670 --> 08:05.710
Slave traders?!

08:05.920 --> 08:07.960
They're a militant group 
that includes war slaves,

08:07.960 --> 08:10.150
magical beasts, and several majin,

08:10.150 --> 08:13.440
and they possess greater military 
might than a small nation...

08:13.950 --> 08:15.220
or they did.

08:15.220 --> 08:17.840
"Did"? Why the past tense?

08:18.130 --> 08:19.970
Apparently, they were wiped out...

08:20.440 --> 08:22.480
by the Lightspeed Hero.

08:24.680 --> 08:27.420
The Lightspeed... Hero?

08:29.170 --> 08:30.970
<i>Okay, I'll see you there.</i>

08:37.060 --> 08:39.430
Yuuki-san worries too much, doesn't he?

08:39.430 --> 08:44.240
Yeah. When Master Masayuki gets serious, 
he has no reason to fear a Demon Lord.

08:44.260 --> 08:46.100
You said it.

08:44.370 --> 08:49.040
<b>Adventurer</b>

08:46.100 --> 08:49.040
You're Masayuki, the Lightspeed Hero!

08:52.560 --> 08:53.460
<i>That's right.</i>

08:53.850 --> 08:56.860
<i>I'm Honjo Masayuki, and I'm a Hero.</i>

08:58.790 --> 09:00.730
Did you do the event gacha yesterday?

09:05.380 --> 09:06.560
Hey, check it out!

09:08.840 --> 09:12.560
<i>One day, I was suddenly sent to this world.</i>

09:12.860 --> 09:16.780
<i>Before I had any idea what was going on, 
I got caught up in an incident.</i>

09:15.110 --> 09:16.420
Help me!

09:20.150 --> 09:26.280
Hey there, bro. You're not tryin' 
to get in my way, are ya?

09:21.120 --> 09:23.980
<i>"That's it. This is the end for me."</i>

09:24.170 --> 09:26.280
<i>That was what I thought...</i>

09:27.450 --> 09:30.900
<i>Heroic, courageous action confirmed.</i>

09:31.590 --> 09:40.550
<b>Unique Skill
Chosen One
Unlocked</b>

09:31.690 --> 09:34.920
<i>Unique skill "Chosen One" unlocked.</i>

09:35.200 --> 09:36.800
<i>Use skill?</i>

09:35.380 --> 09:40.550
<b>Use skill?</b>

09:37.610 --> 09:39.730
Huh? Um... Yes.

09:40.730 --> 09:41.800
<i>Confirmed.</i>

09:40.850 --> 09:42.260
<b>Confirmed</b>

09:42.200 --> 09:45.010
<i>Using Chosen One to acquire language.</i>

09:42.310 --> 09:43.720
<b>Using Chosen One</b>

09:43.770 --> 09:45.180
<b>to acquire language.</b>

09:45.750 --> 09:47.060
<i>Successful.</i>

09:47.060 --> 09:52.070
<b>Unique Skill
Chosen One</b>

09:47.530 --> 09:52.060
<i>And then my unique skill, 
Chosen One, awakened.</i>

09:52.880 --> 09:55.890
Wh-Where'd this intimidating air come from?!

09:56.480 --> 09:59.080
You're no ordinary guy!

09:59.410 --> 10:00.930
<i>Heroic Presence.</i>

10:00.930 --> 10:02.740
<i>A presence projected only by Heroes.</i>

10:02.730 --> 10:06.330
<i>Lesser beings are overwhelmed and 
rendered immobile when it is emitted.</i>

10:08.290 --> 10:10.760
What kinda shady tricks are you using?!

10:10.760 --> 10:12.880
I'll kill you!

10:16.280 --> 10:17.390
Ow...

10:18.890 --> 10:20.370
I don't believe it!

10:20.370 --> 10:23.430
He knocked out Jinrai the Mad Wolf 
without even using his hands!

10:27.890 --> 10:29.650
He dodged his fist by just a hair,

10:29.020 --> 10:30.380
Hey, not bad!

10:29.650 --> 10:31.980
ducked in close, and headbutted him!

10:32.400 --> 10:33.540
He's a master!

10:34.070 --> 10:41.240
<b>Heroic Compensation</b>

10:34.240 --> 10:35.700
<i>Heroic Compensation.</i>

10:35.700 --> 10:39.230
<i>Due to very high luck, all normal attacks, 
as well as attacks by companions,</i>

10:39.230 --> 10:41.230
<i>become critical hits.</i>

10:41.630 --> 10:44.000
I-I underestimated you.

10:44.850 --> 10:46.470
My name's Jinrai.

10:46.470 --> 10:51.000
I was an adventurer known by folks 
around here as the Mad Wolf...

10:51.230 --> 10:53.800
but now I realize I was just full of myself.

10:54.690 --> 10:58.590
Would you please take me 
as your subordinate?

10:59.420 --> 11:02.040
<i>So, even though I hadn't done anything,</i>

11:02.040 --> 11:04.920
<i>Jinrai the Mad Wolf became my companion.</i>

11:06.400 --> 11:08.440
I've heard about you.

11:08.440 --> 11:11.600
So you're an Otherworlder 
who ended up here, too?

11:12.020 --> 11:14.160
People have been calling you a hero,

11:14.160 --> 11:19.140
but if you ask me, you're being 
a bit naïve about this, Masayuki-kun.

11:27.730 --> 11:28.760
Masayuki...

11:29.880 --> 11:32.640
Let me join you, too, Hero Masayuki!

11:32.880 --> 11:34.540
I want to help you!

11:34.540 --> 11:38.680
<i>Heroic Charm. Those who see 
the Hero in action are inspired,</i>

11:38.680 --> 11:42.550
<i>and begin to believe in the Hero 
and want to walk in his footsteps.</i>

11:43.000 --> 11:48.280
<i>So another Otherworlder like me, 
Bernie the Wizard, joined us...</i>

11:48.640 --> 11:52.270
<b>Kingdom of Engrassia
Martial Arts Tournament Arena</b>

11:49.540 --> 11:52.270
You're the one called Masayuki, right?

11:52.640 --> 11:54.870
You're just a scoundrel 
calling yourself a Hero!

12:02.550 --> 12:04.070
<i>Heroic Action.</i>

12:04.070 --> 12:08.400
<i>The Hero's actions set an example 
for his friends and earn him praise.</i>

12:08.580 --> 12:11.910
You are, without a doubt, a true Hero!

12:11.910 --> 12:15.040
Please take me with you, Master Masayuki!

12:15.420 --> 12:18.270
<i>Then Jiwu the Elementalist joined us,</i>

12:18.840 --> 12:21.970
<i>and we became a party of four.</i>

12:27.140 --> 12:33.440
<i>It seems like the unique skill I gained, 
"Chosen One," is pretty rare.</i>

12:33.440 --> 12:36.050
<i>It was Yuuki-san who told me that.</i>

12:36.390 --> 12:39.120
You were the fastest 
in history to reach rank A.

12:39.550 --> 12:41.350
Your sword swings, like flashes of light,

12:41.350 --> 12:43.440
kept you undefeated 
in the martial arts tournament.

12:44.060 --> 12:47.200
You became a Hero in less than a year.

12:47.520 --> 12:51.410
Your accomplishments are remarkable, 
"Lightspeed Hero" Masayuki!

12:51.410 --> 12:56.630
Come on, Yuuki-san, you know it's 
because of Chosen One.

12:56.630 --> 12:59.040
I haven't done a single thing myself.

12:59.040 --> 13:02.630
All of your words and 
actions make those around you

13:02.630 --> 13:06.050
identify you as a Hero all on their own, eh?

13:06.200 --> 13:08.530
That's one incredible power!

13:09.520 --> 13:14.810
So I have a favor to ask of the Hero—
rather, of Team Lightspeed.

13:17.030 --> 13:20.060
The Slave Company... Orthrus?

13:20.320 --> 13:20.800
Yeah.

13:21.160 --> 13:23.620
It's a criminal organization 
working across multiple countries.

13:23.960 --> 13:27.740
They're a notorious group 
that deals in slaves,

13:27.740 --> 13:30.080
drugs, and even dangerous magical beasts.

13:30.290 --> 13:34.580
And the giant market 
where they do their slave trading

13:34.880 --> 13:37.360
has been confirmed to be here, 
in the Kingdom of Ballachia.

13:38.170 --> 13:40.480
I'm impressed you managed to pin them down.

13:40.990 --> 13:43.760
We took in a slave who 
was lucky enough to escape.

13:44.530 --> 13:48.130
So I decided to send people 
to investigate Ballachia.

13:48.440 --> 13:50.680
The projected danger level is B+ or higher.

13:50.680 --> 13:55.120
So it's possible a whole nation is 
involved with them, albeit a small one.

13:55.400 --> 13:57.790
The investigators will have to be subtle.

13:57.790 --> 14:01.680
That's a bit much to ask of 
adventurers who only know how to fight.

14:02.240 --> 14:04.260
Yet if I send the investigators alone,

14:04.260 --> 14:07.190
I'm not sure if they'll 
be able to make contact.

14:07.640 --> 14:10.690
That's why I'd like you guys 
to go with them.

14:11.180 --> 14:14.060
I want you to keep the leadership 
of Ballachia distracted

14:14.060 --> 14:16.810
while the investigators are nabbing 
evidence of their slave trade.

14:18.830 --> 14:20.160
So we're decoys?

14:20.710 --> 14:23.410
I wanted to refuse their request,

14:23.410 --> 14:26.010
but I can't go against 
the will of our sponsors.

14:26.240 --> 14:29.880
Masayuki, let's help them out!

14:29.880 --> 14:33.120
And hey, if it leads to war,

14:33.120 --> 14:35.480
we can beat a small nation 
like that on our own!

14:35.480 --> 14:36.530
I agree.

14:36.530 --> 14:39.270
Slavery shouldn't be 
allowed in this day and age.

14:39.270 --> 14:43.450
I'm sure Masayuki-kun's power will 
convert them to the side of justice.

14:43.450 --> 14:44.540
Master Masayuki.

14:45.480 --> 14:48.520
I will abide by your decision.

14:51.840 --> 14:54.480
All right. We'll go.

14:55.540 --> 14:57.680
I had a feeling you'd say that!

14:57.950 --> 14:59.620
Okay, I'll explain the plan.

14:58.560 --> 15:02.530
<i>Yuuki-san has done a lot for me 
since I came to this world, after all.</i>

15:02.820 --> 15:04.900
<i>There was no way I could refuse.</i>

15:07.320 --> 15:09.350
<i>Then we arrived in the Kingdom of Ballachia.</i>

15:09.810 --> 15:14.140
<i>Even there, I was constantly 
at the whim of Chosen One.</i>

15:15.120 --> 15:17.310
Well, well!

15:17.590 --> 15:22.560
What an honor to meet the Lightspeed Hero, 
whose name is known around the world!

15:22.780 --> 15:25.430
Please, enjoy your stay here.

15:25.430 --> 15:28.120
Ah... I will. Thank you.

15:28.120 --> 15:32.100
Do try to refrain from offending 
the Hero, Count Braver.

15:32.100 --> 15:35.870
Of course, Duke Gosel. 
I will keep that in mind.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.250
Masayuki-kun's taking a while.

15:44.250 --> 15:48.050
Think he got lost on the way 
back from the bathroom?

15:48.050 --> 15:50.050
I hope he's okay...

15:53.070 --> 15:55.870
U-Um, where is the bathroom?

15:56.490 --> 16:01.040
Well, well. If it isn't the Lightspeed Hero.

16:01.040 --> 16:04.400
To think you would show up at the 
very moment we were signing...

16:04.400 --> 16:06.650
a slave trade contract!

16:06.650 --> 16:09.600
The bathroom... Wait, slaves?!

16:09.800 --> 16:13.610
I had a very strong soldier stand 
outside to prevent interruption...

16:13.890 --> 16:16.330
I suppose I should have 
expected no less of the Hero.

16:16.330 --> 16:19.040
Wait... I didn't see anyone like that!

16:19.240 --> 16:21.970
Now that you've seen us, 
we are left with no choice.

16:35.200 --> 16:37.940
Oh, no! The Hero has gone mad!

16:37.940 --> 16:38.300
Huh?!

16:38.300 --> 16:40.050
We cannot let this stand!

16:40.050 --> 16:43.040
Men, get in here! Now!

16:52.440 --> 16:56.480
Punks like you aren't 
even worth Masayuki's time.

16:56.480 --> 16:58.560
Masayuki-kun, what happened?

17:00.670 --> 17:03.200
This situation, this tragedy...

17:03.200 --> 17:05.630
What do you think happened?

17:05.630 --> 17:08.370
I see. So that's it.

17:08.370 --> 17:10.220
This is bad, Masayuki!

17:10.220 --> 17:12.210
We're in the Kingdom of Ballachia!

17:12.210 --> 17:14.970
Even if the Hero's renown 
has spread far and wide,

17:14.970 --> 17:17.720
if Duke Gosel frames you for a crime...

17:18.200 --> 17:19.760
Eh, it'll be fine.

17:25.070 --> 17:26.270
Master Masayuki!

17:26.560 --> 17:29.440
This man is a valuable witness, right?

17:29.440 --> 17:33.280
He was still alive, 
so I healed him with magic!

17:33.280 --> 17:35.780
Wh-What happened to me?

17:35.780 --> 17:36.870
Yo, old man!

17:38.790 --> 17:41.380
If you'll give us an honest testimony,

17:41.380 --> 17:43.830
you'll only be charged with slave trading.

17:44.200 --> 17:46.290
But if you keep secrets,

17:46.290 --> 17:50.080
that guy there is just gonna kill you again.

17:50.580 --> 17:52.780
So what'll it be?

17:53.290 --> 17:55.600
What is going on in here?!

17:56.800 --> 17:59.510
<i>The king just happened 
to show up at that moment.</i>

18:00.000 --> 18:00.830
<i>That's right.</i>

18:00.830 --> 18:04.390
<i>Chosen One puts things in order 
with frightening efficiency</i>

18:04.390 --> 18:07.770
<i>and just walks me right into being the Hero.</i>

18:09.570 --> 18:12.480
<i>After that, things took a very rapid turn.</i>

18:14.140 --> 18:19.630
<i>It was revealed that Duke Gosel was a 
leader in the criminal organization Orthrus.</i>

18:19.880 --> 18:25.740
<i>Not only that, but it became clear 
that Orthrus's base was here in Ballachia.</i>

18:26.870 --> 18:31.600
I can't believe those slave traders were using 
Ballachia as a front for their dirty business!

18:31.600 --> 18:34.500
I absolutely cannot accept this!

18:34.700 --> 18:36.760
Hero Masayuki!

18:36.760 --> 18:40.750
Please assist me in eliminating Orthrus!

18:41.380 --> 18:44.020
<i>Yeah, of course it would lead to this...</i>

18:48.640 --> 18:52.280
<i>Thus the operation to 
eliminate Orthrus commenced.</i>

19:04.590 --> 19:08.820
<i>Every last one of the 
slave traders was purged.</i>

19:09.120 --> 19:12.290
Under the influence of your Chosen One,

19:12.290 --> 19:16.410
everyone around suddenly 
displays incredible strength.

19:17.620 --> 19:21.480
<i>And like always, this incident 
that broke out on its own</i>

19:21.480 --> 19:23.560
<i>ended while all I did was stand there,</i>

19:23.560 --> 19:27.370
<i>and my reputation as the 
Hero spread even farther.</i>

19:28.240 --> 19:31.610
<i>But just one part of it all 
turned out differently...</i>

19:32.330 --> 19:34.230
Hero Masayuki...

19:34.230 --> 19:37.490
Please! Please lend me your strength!

19:37.490 --> 19:39.730
You're asking me?!

19:40.020 --> 19:43.280
What do you expect me to do 
with all the elves you've taken in?

19:43.510 --> 19:47.740
They wish to return to their home 
in the Great Forest of Jura,

19:47.740 --> 19:50.800
but I cannot just set 
them free in that forest.

19:51.090 --> 19:52.120
Why not?

19:52.400 --> 19:57.760
Because the Great Forest of Jura 
is Demon Lord Rimuru's territory now.

19:58.160 --> 20:01.720
If the elves complained to him about 
the evil deeds of the humans...

20:01.720 --> 20:04.390
He might come looking for revenge, huh?

20:04.390 --> 20:05.880
Correct.

20:05.880 --> 20:11.520
But Ballachia cannot walk 
the same path Falmuth did!

20:11.940 --> 20:14.520
So please... please...

20:14.520 --> 20:16.240
Okay, okay!

20:16.240 --> 20:20.760
We'll take the elves to 
the Great Forest of Jura.

20:21.650 --> 20:24.920
Y-You have my gratitude, Hero Masayuki!

20:24.920 --> 20:27.360
<i>I'm just taking some elves to a forest...</i>

20:27.360 --> 20:28.550
<i>It'll be fine, right?</i>

20:29.240 --> 20:31.040
<i>At least, that's what I thought...</i>

20:31.040 --> 20:33.040
What?!

20:33.040 --> 20:35.960
Masayuki the Hero is going to Tempest!

20:35.960 --> 20:38.710
Hero Masayuki is finally setting 
out to slay a Demon Lord?!

20:38.970 --> 20:41.550
Now that Lady Hinata has 
fallen to Demon Lord Rimuru,

20:41.550 --> 20:44.040
Hero Masayuki is this world's only hope!

20:44.040 --> 20:45.770
Hero Masayuki!

20:45.770 --> 20:47.050
Hero Masayuki!

20:49.440 --> 20:52.550
<i>And this somehow turned into a big deal...</i>

20:58.940 --> 21:03.040
I'm not even going there 
to fight Demon Lord Rimuru...

21:03.490 --> 21:06.100
And it's not like Hinata-san lost to him.

21:06.100 --> 21:07.200
Well...

21:07.200 --> 21:11.450
There are probably some people who 
find it more convenient to say she lost.

21:11.810 --> 21:15.880
That said, the fact that he and 
Hinata the Saint ended up in a draw...

21:16.390 --> 21:17.960
Demon Lord Rimuru...

21:18.340 --> 21:20.440
We should probably keep 
our guard up with him.

21:20.440 --> 21:24.510
When Master Masayuki gets serious, 
he has no reason to fear a Demon Lord!

21:25.250 --> 21:29.180
But I've also heard that he wants 
to be friends with humans.

21:30.320 --> 21:32.750
Maybe we should just 
see how things go first.

21:33.820 --> 21:35.040
I get it!

21:35.040 --> 21:37.100
Yes, you might be right!

21:37.100 --> 21:39.810
I will abide by your decision, Master Masayuki!

21:39.810 --> 21:41.600
So will I!

21:39.810 --> 21:41.600
Master Masayuki!

21:41.600 --> 21:43.640
<i>Well, I'm sure it'll all work out.</i>

21:45.110 --> 21:47.560
<i>I can't stop Chosen One.</i>

21:47.860 --> 21:50.080
<i>I wouldn't even know how to.</i>

21:52.670 --> 21:56.220
The Lightspeed Hero Masayuki, eh?

21:57.720 --> 21:59.290
What shall we do?

21:59.290 --> 22:02.790
I'm willing to get rid of him 
before he can cause trouble.

22:02.790 --> 22:03.290
Huh?!

22:03.290 --> 22:06.550
If he's truly talking nonsense 
about slaying a Demon Lord,

22:06.790 --> 22:09.290
I will ensure that he learns his place.

22:09.290 --> 22:11.840
Oh, I would be happy to handle that job!

22:13.040 --> 22:14.750
The Lightspeed Hero...

22:14.750 --> 22:17.300
Perhaps he will provide some entertainment.

22:18.740 --> 22:19.890
Great Rimuru...

22:20.270 --> 22:22.930
The Opening Festival is 
an important national event.

22:22.930 --> 22:26.630
You must avoid stirring up conflict 
with the Hero at this time.

22:27.030 --> 22:28.810
I know, I know.

22:29.120 --> 22:32.090
It's a fact that he freed 
the elf slaves, anyway.

22:32.090 --> 22:34.280
I'll meet with him 
and talk to him, at least.

22:34.660 --> 22:38.270
So, on that note, I will 
handle the Hero Masayuki.

22:38.270 --> 22:40.300
No interfering! Got it?

22:40.300 --> 22:41.240
What?!

22:41.240 --> 22:42.240
Got it?!

22:42.240 --> 22:43.700
Yes, sir!

22:48.120 --> 22:50.630
<i>The festival starts in three days,</i>

22:50.630 --> 22:52.770
<i>and now even more trouble is coming...</i>

24:25.230 --> 24:28.820
<i>Next time, "Digression: Luminus Memories."</i>

24:25.980 --> 24:29.940
<b>Digression :<u>Luminus Memories</u></b>
